Error: failed to open database: database "velvet_ballistics" not found on Dolt server at 127.0.0.1:37481

Common causes:
  - Switched git branches (the Dolt database is runtime state, not in git)
  - The server is serving a different data directory than expected
  - The server was restarted and is using a different port
  - Another project's Dolt server is running on this port

To diagnose:
  bd doctor                  # Check server and database health
  bd dolt status             # Show which data directory the server is using

Tip: If this is an existing project, fresh clone, or shared-server recovery, run bd bootstrap first.
If bootstrap cannot find the expected remote automatically, set sync.git-remote
in .beads/config.yaml and re-run bd bootstrap.
Use bd bootstrap --dry-run if you need to confirm the plan before it initializes anything.
Use bd init only when creating a brand-new project with no existing .beads data.
